Simple One Server Web Infrastructure

How it works?

-The browser ask the DNS system: Where is www.foobar.com
-DNS answer: Its at IP addres 8.8.8.8.
-The browser connects to that Ip wich is your server
-The server has Nginx installed (the web server)
-The application server runs your code (the app files)
-If your code needs data it ask th MySQL db
-The database returns the information the app builds the response and Nginx delivers it back to the users browser

Key pieces Explained

-Server -> a physical or virtual computer that provides services to users over the internet. In this case it runs the web server, app server and database all in the box
-Domain name -> a human friendly way to reach your site (foobar.com) instead of typing the raw IP addres 8.8.8.8
-DNS record -> the www in www.foobar.com is a A record. servers staic files and forwards dynamic request to the app.
-Application server -> runs the actual business logic (your code base)
-Database (MySQL) -> stores and organizes the data the app needs (users, orders, messages, etc.)
Communication -> the server and the user computer talk over the internet using TCP/IP. The website itself is usually served over HTTP or HTTPS
